course: dictionary
lesson: 339
title: Announce
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To announce something is to tell it publicly, so that lots of people know. Context gives you clues. «When a test is announced, revising a little on several different days works better than cramming the night before.» The announced test is news that everyone is told about, so announced means told officially.
explain: «Poppy hugs her new bunny and announces: "Snowy's getting a carrot every single day, because rabbits LOVE carrots!"» The capital letters and the word "because" show she says it firmly and loudly, sure of herself. So to announce can mean to say something firmly so everyone hears.
explain: «Theo's grandma sent twenty pounds in cash, and Theo announced it was all going on games.» Swap in a simpler word: Theo told it was all going on games still makes sense. Announced here means told, the same as the clue in the sentence.
fact: To announce means to tell people something officially or publicly.
fact: To announce can also mean to say something firmly or loudly so everyone hears.
fact: To announce can mean to tell people that someone has arrived or that something will happen.
fact: The phrase «make an announcement» means to tell people something important.
fact: Announcements are made at train stations, at airports, and by the head teacher in assembly.
exercise: «Theo's grandma sent twenty pounds in cash, and Theo announced it was all going on games.» What does announced mean here? | *Said it out loud to everyone | Lost it in the park | Counted it twice | Hid it under the bed
exercise: Poppy announces, «Snowy's getting a carrot every single day!» How does she say it? | Sadly, with a tear in her eye | Shyly, looking at the floor | *Firmly and loudly, sure of herself | Quietly, in a whisper
exercise: Which phrase means to tell people something important? | *Make an announcement | Make a mess | Make a wish | Make a face
test:
«When a test is announced, revising a little on several different days works better than cramming.» What does announced mean? | Cancelled | *Officially told to people | Hidden in a box | Drawn on a board
Which places often have announcements for travellers? | Swimming pools | Pet shops | *Train stations and airports | Farms
exam:
In «Theo announced it was all going on games», which word could replace announced with almost the same meaning? | ate | *told | slept | forgot
